{
  "workflowId": "300000331058430",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_PRJ_PROJECT_FINANCIAL_CONTROL_AGENT",
  "name": "Project Financial Control Agent",
  "description": "Manages the financial lifecycle of projects with proactive oversight to keep costs, billing, revenue, assets, and accounting reconciliations on track. Cross-checks project financials against enterprise financial records to catch discrepancies early and reduce reporting errors. Provides real-time insights and guided workflows for issue resolution, accelerating financial management from project initiation to close-out.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [
      {
        "id": "routingContext",
        "name": "routingContext",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778502332338"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Relevant Information",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "// 1. Parse atomic agent output safely.\nlet pfcaRaw = $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvAtomicAgentOutput;\nlet pfca = {};\n\ntry {\n    pfca = (typeof pfcaRaw === 'string') ? JSON.parse(pfcaRaw) : (pfcaRaw || {});\n} catch (e) {\n    pfca = {};\n}\n\n// 2. Parse stored active atomic-agent details safely for follow-up fallback.\nlet activeDetailsVar = $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails;\nlet activeDetailsRaw = {};\n\nif (activeDetailsVar && typeof activeDetailsVar === 'object') {\n    activeDetailsRaw = activeDetailsVar.ActiveAtomicAgentDetails || activeDetailsVar;\n} else if (typeof activeDetailsVar === 'string' && activeDetailsVar.trim() !== '') {\n    try {\n        let parsed = JSON.parse(activeDetailsVar);\n        activeDetailsRaw = parsed.ActiveAtomicAgentDetails || parsed;\n    } catch (e) {\n        activeDetailsRaw = {};\n    }\n}\n\nconst isPresent = value => value !== null && value !== undefined;\n\nconst getFlexKey = (obj, keyName) => {\n    if (!obj || typeof obj !== 'object') return null;\n    const escapedKey = keyName.replace(/_/g, '\\\\_');\n    return isPresent(obj[keyName]) ? obj[keyName] : obj[escapedKey];\n};\n\nconst getValue = (primaryObj, fallbackObj, keyName) => {\n    let primaryValue = getFlexKey(primaryObj, keyName);\n    let fallbackValue = getFlexKey(fallbackObj, keyName);\n    return isPresent(primaryValue) ? primaryValue : (isPresent(fallbackValue) ? fallbackValue : null);\n};\n\nconst asObject = value => {\n    if (!isPresent(value)) return {};\n    if (typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value)) return value;\n    if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim() !== '') {\n        try {\n            let parsed = JSON.parse(value);\n            return parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : {};\n        } catch (e) {\n            return {};\n        }\n    }\n    return {};\n};\n\nconst asArray = value => {\n    if (Array.isArray(value)) return value;\n    if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim() !== '') {\n        try {\n            let parsed = JSON.parse(value);\n            return Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : [];\n        } catch (e) {\n            return [];\n        }\n    }\n    return [];\n};\n\nconst mergeObjectValues = (primaryObj, fallbackObj) => {\n    let primary = asObject(primaryObj);\n    let fallback = asObject(fallbackObj);\n    let merged = {};\n    let keys = new Set([...Object.keys(fallback), ...Object.keys(primary)]);\n\n    keys.forEach(key => {\n        let primaryValue = getFlexKey(primary, key);\n        let fallbackValue = getFlexKey(fallback, key);\n        merged[key] = isPresent(primaryValue) ? primaryValue : (isPresent(fallbackValue) ? fallbackValue : null);\n    });\n\n    return merged;\n};\n\nconst getActionLabel = label => {\n    if (!isPresent(label)) return 'actions';\n    let cleanLabel = String(label).trim();\n    return cleanLabel !== '' ? cleanLabel : 'actions';\n};\n\nconst addActionItems = (target, label, items) => {\n    let actionLabel = getActionLabel(label);\n\n    if (!target[actionLabel]) {\n        target[actionLabel] = { items: [] };\n    }\n\n    if (!Array.isArray(target[actionLabel].items)) {\n        target[actionLabel].items = [];\n    }\n\n    items.forEach(entry => {\n        target[actionLabel].items.push(entry);\n    });\n};\n\nconst extractActionPayload = item => {\n    let actionPayload = {};\n\n    const visit = (node, parentKey) => {\n        if (!isPresent(node)) return;\n\n        if (Array.isArray(node)) {\n            node.forEach(entry => visit(entry, parentKey));\n            return;\n        }\n\n        if (typeof node !== 'object') return;\n\n        Object.keys(node).forEach(key => {\n            let childValue = node[key];\n\n            if (key === 'items' && Array.isArray(childValue)) {\n                let actionLabel = getActionLabel(parentKey);\n                addActionItems(actionPayload, actionLabel, childValue);\n\n                childValue.forEach(entry => {\n                    visit(entry, actionLabel);\n                });\n\n                return;\n            }\n\n            visit(childValue, key);\n        });\n    };\n\n    visit(item, null);\n    return actionPayload;\n};\n\nconst normalizeFallbackAtomicAgentResponse = fallbackResponse => {\n    let fallback = asObject(fallbackResponse);\n    let normalized = {};\n    let textIndex = 1;\n    let tableIndex = 1;\n    let listIndex = 1;\n    let actionIndex = 1;\n    let keys = Object.keys(fallback).sort();\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < keys.length; i++) {\n        let key = keys[i];\n        let value = fallback[key];\n\n        if (/^text\\d+$/.test(key) && isPresent(value)) {\n            normalized[key] = value;\n            let n = parseInt(key.replace('text', ''), 10);\n            if (!isNaN(n) && n >= textIndex) textIndex = n + 1;\n        }\n\n        if (/^table\\d+$/.test(key) && isPresent(value)) {\n            normalized[key] = value;\n            let n = parseInt(key.replace('table', ''), 10);\n            if (!isNaN(n) && n >= tableIndex) tableIndex = n + 1;\n        }\n\n        if (/^list\\d+$/.test(key) && isPresent(value)) {\n            normalized[key] = value;\n            let n = parseInt(key.replace('list', ''), 10);\n            if (!isNaN(n) && n >= listIndex) listIndex = n + 1;\n        }\n\n        if (/^action\\d+$/.test(key) && isPresent(value)) {\n            normalized[key] = extractActionPayload(value);\n            let n = parseInt(key.replace('action', ''), 10);\n            if (!isNaN(n) && n >= actionIndex) actionIndex = n + 1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (isPresent(fallback.text) && !isPresent(normalized.text1)) {\n        normalized['text' + textIndex] = fallback.text;\n    }\n\n    if (isPresent(fallback.table) && !isPresent(normalized.table1)) {\n        normalized['table' + tableIndex] = fallback.table;\n    }\n\n    if (isPresent(fallback.list) && !isPresent(normalized.list1)) {\n        normalized['list' + listIndex] = fallback.list;\n    }\n\n    if (isPresent(fallback.action) && !isPresent(normalized.action1)) {\n        normalized['action' + actionIndex] = extractActionPayload(fallback.action);\n    }\n\n    return normalized;\n};\n\nconst buildAtomicAgentResponse = (agentResponse, fallbackResponse) => {\n    let response = {};\n    let textIndex = 1;\n    let tableIndex = 1;\n    let listIndex = 1;\n    let actionIndex = 1;\n    let items = asArray(agentResponse);\n    let fallback = normalizeFallbackAtomicAgentResponse(fallbackResponse);\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n        let item = items[i] || {};\n        let displayType = String(item.display_type || '').toLowerCase();\n\n        if (displayType === 'text' && isPresent(item.text)) {\n            response['text' + textIndex] = String(item.text);\n            textIndex++;\n        }\n\n        if (displayType === 'table') {\n            response['table' + tableIndex] = isPresent(item.rows) ? item.rows : {};\n            tableIndex++;\n        }\n\n        if (displayType === 'list') {\n            response['list' + listIndex] = isPresent(item.fields) ? item.fields : {};\n            listIndex++;\n        }\n\n        if (displayType === 'action') {\n            response['action' + actionIndex] = extractActionPayload(item);\n            actionIndex++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (const key of Object.keys(fallback)) {\n        if (!isPresent(response[key])) {\n            response[key] = fallback[key];\n        }\n    }\n\n    return response;\n};\n\n// 3. Extract current atomic-agent details. Keep older key support only as fallback.\nconst atomicAgentDetails = asObject(\n    getFlexKey(pfca, 'atomicAgentDetails') ||\n    getFlexKey(pfca, 'relevant_info')\n);\nconst fallbackDetails = asObject(activeDetailsRaw);\n\nconst currentContextDetails = asObject(\n    getFlexKey(atomicAgentDetails, 'contextDetails') ||\n    getFlexKey(atomicAgentDetails, 'ContextualParameters')\n);\nconst fallbackContextDetails = asObject(\n    getFlexKey(fallbackDetails, 'contextDetails') ||\n    getFlexKey(fallbackDetails, 'ContextualParameters')\n);\nconst contextDetails = mergeObjectValues(currentContextDetails, fallbackContextDetails);\n\nconst atomicAgentResponse = buildAtomicAgentResponse(\n    getFlexKey(pfca, 'agent_response'),\n    getFlexKey(fallbackDetails, 'atomicAgentResponse')\n);\n\n// 4. Return the ActiveAtomicAgentDetails structure used by the orchestrator.\nreturn {\n    atomicAgentCode: getValue(atomicAgentDetails, fallbackDetails, 'atomicAgentCode') ||\n        getValue(atomicAgentDetails, fallbackDetails, 'atomicAgentName'),\n    atomicAgentContext: getValue(atomicAgentDetails, fallbackDetails, 'atomicAgentContext') ||\n        getValue(atomicAgentDetails, fallbackDetails, 'AtomicAgentState'),\n    contextDetails: contextDetails,\n    filters: getValue(atomicAgentDetails, fallbackDetails, 'filters') ||\n        getValue(atomicAgentDetails, fallbackDetails, 'FiltersApplied'),\n    atomicAgentResponse: atomicAgentResponse\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777352422206"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_CODE_EXTRACT_RELEVANT_INFORMATION",
          "id": "1778502332338",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Multi Turn Conversation Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780305806740"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_SET_VARIABLE_SET_MULTI_TURN_CONVERSATION_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1777352422206",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777352422206_prjPjcVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails",
              "name": "prjPjcVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_CODE_EXTRACT_RELEVANT_INFORMATION.$output.result}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1777352422206_prjPjcVarConvRoutingContext",
              "name": "prjPjcVarConvRoutingContext",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.routingContext}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75,
                "temperature": 0.01,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "description": "Classifies a PFCA request for Level 2 assistant routing across Cost Management, Asset Management, Project Accounting, Project Billing, unsupported, and off-topic branches.",
            "name": "Intent Identification"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780305170352"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_LLM_PFCA_INTENT_RECOGNIZER",
          "id": "1777353863021",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777353863021_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the ***Intent Identification*** component for the Project Financial Control Agent (PFCA).\nThe Project Financial Control Agent (PFCA) enables users to monitor, analyze, and manage project financials (costs, revenue, billing, capitalization, accounting reconciliation) through natural language interactions. The agent helps manage the financial lifecycle of projects with proactive oversight to keep costs, billing, revenue, assets, and accounting reconciliations on track. Cross-checks project financials against enterprise financial records to catch discrepancies early and reduce reporting errors. Provides real-time insights and guided workflows for issue resolution, accelerating financial management from project initiation to close-out.\n\nInputs:\n- Current user query: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvModifiedQuery}}\n- Active atomic-agent details: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails}}\n- CurrentContext: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}}\n\nTask:\nClassify the current user request for Level 2 assistant routing.\nYour job is to classify the user's request and route it to ***exactly one*** worker agent.\nDo not answer the user's question.\nDo not perform financial analysis.\nDo not ask follow-up questions unless the request is impossible to classify.\n\n\nAvailable routes:\n\nThe chosen route can be ***EXACTLY*** of the following:\n- \"Project Financial Inquiry\"\n- \"Project Cost Management\"\n- \"Project Asset Capitalization\"\n- \"Project Accounting Reconciliation\"\n- \"Project Bill Transactions Management\"\n- \"Project Invoice Management\"\n- \"Payroll Distribution Assistant\"\n- \"Help Topic\"\n- \"Unsupported\"\n- \"Off Topic\"\n\nTerminology normalization:\nTreat the following phrases as equivalent to the canonical terms below:\n\nCanonical term: Project Cost Transaction\nAliases include:\n- project cost\n- cost record\n- cost transaction\n- cost txn\n- project cost txn\n- project expenditure\n- expenditure item\n- exp item\n- project actual\n- incurred cost\n\nCanonical term: Unprocessed Project Cost Transaction\nAliases include:\n- unprocessed project cost\n- unprocessed cost\n- unprocessed transaction\n- unprocessed txn\n- pending cost\n- cost awaiting import\n- pending project cost\n- cost not yet processed\n- staged cost\n\nCanonical term: Bill Transaction\nAliases include:\n- WIP transaction\n- Billing transaction\n- Bill txn\n- Bill trx\n- Billing event\n\nCanonical term: Project Contract Invoice\nAliases include:\n- Project bill\n- Contract bill\n- Customer invoice\n- Customer invoice\n- Customer bill\n- Project services invoice\n\nCanonical term: Project Asset\nAliases include:\n- CIP asset\n- Project-built asset\n- Capital project asset\n- Construction-in-progress asset\n- WIP asset\n- Work-in-progress asset\n\nCanonical term: Project Asset Line\nAliases include:\n- Project asset cost line\n- Asset cost line\n- Capitalization line\n\nRouting rule:\nWhen a user request uses an alias, classify it as if the canonical term had been used.\n\nAvailable Routes:\n1. Project Financial Inquiry\nUse for:\n- inquiries related to project cost transactions, unprocessed project cost transactions, project assets, project asset lines, and project asset line assignments (excluding questions on getting / viewing / fetching pending capitalization costs , uncapitalized costs). All inquiry requests for other business objects are currently not supported by the Project Financial Inquiry agent.\n- IMPORTANT: this route doesn't handle any queries related to EXCEPTIONS.\n- IMPORTANT: this route doesn't handle any queries related to viewing/retrieving/fetching project cost transactions based on their capitalization processing status. For example:\n\tRequest: \"Show me the uncapitalized costs on project Orion.\" \n\tResult: Not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\tReason: Request is related to the capitalization processing status of the project cost transactions. This type of request is not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\t\n\tRequest: \"Show me the capitalized costs on project Orion.\"\n\tResult: Not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\tReason: Request is related to the capitalization processing status of the project cost transactions. This type of request is not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\n\tRequest: \"Show me the capitalizable costs on project Orion.\"\n\tResult: This request is valid for the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\tReason: Request is related to the capitalizable attribute of a project cost transaction (Yes/No). It isn't related to the capitalization processing status (capitalized or uncapitalized). Hence, it's valid for the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n- IMPORTANT: this route doesn't handle any queries related to viewing/retrieving/fetching project cost transactions based on their invoicing/billing processing status. For example:\n\tRequest: \"Show me the unbilled project costs on project Orion.\" \n\tResult: Not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\tReason: Request is related to the invoicing/billing processing status of the project cost transactions. This type of request is not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\t\n\tRequest: \"Show me the billed transactions on project Orion.\"\n\tResult: Not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\tReason: Request is related to the invoicing/billing processing status of bill transactions. This type of request is not handled by the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\n\tRequest: \"Show me the billable costs on project Orion.\"\n\tResult: This request is valid for the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\tReason: Request is related to the billable attribute of a project cost transaction (Yes/No). It isn't related to the invoicing/billing processing status (billed, invoiced, unbilled, WIP, uninvoiced). Hence, it's valid for the Project Financial Inquiry route.\n\t\n- inquiries are based on list/count/status. Requests related to root cause/why/failure analysis are not handled by Project Financial Inquiry.\n- IMPORTANT: this route handles INQUIRY requests only. Any requests to perform an action, indicated by key words such as - update, adjust, submit, delete, create, approve, submit, transfer, import, and so on - are outside of the scope of the Project Financial Inquiry agent.   \n\n2. Project Cost Management\nUse for: \n- questions about project cost exceptions or unprocessed project cost exceptions.\n- IMPORTANT: If the user's request doesn't clearly indicate cost exceptions, don't use this route. \nFor example:\nUser's Request: \"Show exceptions for Project Gemini.\"\nOutcome: This request should not be routed to Project Cost Management because the request doesn't clearly indicate cost exceptions. The user's request could refer to billing exceptions, capitalizable exceptions, or any other types of exceptions. \n\n3. Project Asset Capitalization\nUse for: \n- questions related to why project costs haven't been capitalized.\n- questions seeking diagnostic explanations regarding the results of the project asset capitalization process.\n- questions related to capitalized or uncapitalized (CIP, construction-in-progress, construction-in-process, pending capitalization) costs.\n- questions related to capitalizable project costs or capitalizable unprocessed project costs shouldn't be routed to Project Asset Capitalization.\n\n4. Project Accounting Reconciliation\nUse for:\n- questions about differences between project accounting and general ledger.\n- questions related to the accounting processing status (unaccounted or accounted) of project costs.\n\n5. Project Bill Transactions Management\nUse for:\n   - The request is clearly about bill transactions.\n   - The user mentions bill transactions, cost bill transactions, event bill transactions, bill transaction exceptions or errors\n   - The user asks for status of bill transactions, such as: \n\t\t\"What is my unbilled balance for Contract Velocity?\"\n\t\t\"What is my WIP balance for Contract Velocity?\"\n   - The request is a clear follow-up to an existing Bill Transaction Management response.\n\n6.Project Invoice Management\n  Use for:\n   - The request is clearly about project contract invoices.\n   - The user mentions invoices, invoice actions such as submit, approve, release, transfer, accept, revert, invoice exceptions or errors\n   - The request is a clear follow-up to an existing Project Invoice Management response.\n\n7.Payroll Distribution Assistant\n  Use for:\n   - The request is related to the inquiry of labor schedules used in Labor Distribution.\n   - The request is for a simulation of what would be the results of an input payroll amount, for a given date and worker.\n   - The Payroll Distribution Assistant doesn't answer questions related to actual payroll costs or actual payroll cost distribution details.\n   - This assistant can't perform any actions on labor schedules. Therefore, action requests related to labor schedules are not handled by this assistant. Examples of the action requests relevant to labor schedules but not supported by this assistant are:\n\t\"Create a new labor schedule for Bella Clarkson starting on June 1, 2026\"\n\t\"Update Bella Clarkson's labor schedule distribution for Project Orion to 80%\"\n\t\"Delete the NEW labor schedule for Jackson Bennett for June 2026\"\n \t\"Approve the NEW labor schedule for Jackson Bennett that begins on June 1, 2026\"\n\n8. Help Topic\nUse when the user asks how to use the PFCA, what the agent can do, topics relevant for project financial control, examples of supported questions, or navigation help.\n\n9. Unsupported\nUse when:\n- the request is related to project financial control topics but can't be handled by any current worker agent.\n\n10. Off Topic\nUse when: \n- the request is unrelated to project financial control.\n- the request is casual chatter, invalid, or too vague to safely interpret as a PFCA request.\n- the request can't be routed confidently to any of the previous available routes. \n\nClassification rules:\n\n1. If the request is unrelated to project financial control, route to ***Off Topic***.\n2. If the request is casual chatter, invalid, or too vague to identify a project financial control intent, route to ***Off Topic***.\n3. If the user asks how to use PFCA, what PFCA can do, what questions are supported, or how to navigate the agent, route to ***Help Topic***.\n4. If the request asks the agent to perform an action such as create, update, adjust, submit, delete, approve, transfer, import, or post, route to ***Unsupported*** unless one of the current worker agents explicitly supports that action.\n5. If the request includes phrases such as \"Generate a summary\" or \"Generate a report\", then this is a valid Project Financial Inquiry request. However, if the request includes phrases such as \"Generate Invoices\", \"Generate Revenue\", \"Generate Asset Lines\", then this is a request for an action, and it's currently not supported. Therefore, it should be routed to ***Unsupported***.\n6. If the request is about a project financial control topic but the relevant business object is not currently supported by any worker agent, route to ***Unsupported***.\n7. If the request is about project cost exceptions or unprocessed project cost exceptions, route to ***Project Cost Management***, even if the request also mentions project costs or unprocessed project costs. If the request includes exceptions, but doesn't clearly specify as cost exceptions, do not assume it is for costs and do not route to *** Project Cost Management***.\n8. If the request asks why capitalizable project costs, asset lines, or project assets have not been capitalized, generated, transferred, or processed, route to ***Project Asset Capitalization***.\n9. If the request asks about differences, mismatches, variances, unreconciled amounts, or reconciliation between project accounting and the general ledger, route to ***Project Accounting Reconciliation***.\n10. If the request is about bill transactions, cost bill transactions, event bill transactions, bill transaction exceptions or errors, route to ***Project Bill Transactions Management***.\n11. If the request is about invoices, invoice actions such as submit, approve, release, transfer, accept, revert, invoice exceptions or errors, route to ***Project Invoice Management***.\n12. If the request is an inquiry about supported Project Financial Inquiry business objects, route to Project Financial Inquiry unless a more specific route above applies.\n13. Specific exception, diagnostic, reconciliation, billing, or revenue intents override general Project Financial Inquiry.\n14. If a request contains multiple intents that map to different worker agents, route to the agent responsible for the more specific diagnostic or exception-oriented intent. If there is no clear dominant intent, route to ***Unsupported***.\n15. If a request uses ambiguous terms, prefer the route indicated by the business object and task, not by isolated keywords.\n16. If the request is project financial control-related but unclear, route to ***Unsupported***. If the request is clearly not project financial control-related, route to ***Off Topic***.\n17. If the user request has \"unprocessed transactions\" keyword without any capital or asset keyword, override the prior context and always strictly route to ***Project Financial Inquiry***.\n18. If the user requests exception or error transactions, but doesn't specify the type of exception/error (project unprocessed cost, project cost, bill transaction, project contract invoice, unaccounted, or capitalization), then this is ambiguous and should route to ***Unsupported***. EXCEPTION TO THIS RULE: If the {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}} is Project Accounting Reconciliation, then route to *** Project Accounting Reconciliation ***.\n19. If the user requests to see transactions, but doesn't specify the type of transaction (project cost, project unprocessed cost, bill transaction, project contract invoice, unaccounted, and so on), then this is ambiguous and should route to ***Unsupported***. EXCEPTION TO THIS RULE: If the {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}} is Project Accounting Reconciliation, then route to *** Project Accounting Reconciliation ***.\n20. If the user requests modifications to a displayed table or previous filter criteria, then route to the current context {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}}. \nFor example: \nInitial User Request: \"Show me cost exceptions for Project Orion and cost type Professional.\" \nCurrent Request:  \"Remove cost type\" \nThis is a valid follow up instruction. The user's intent is to remove the cost type filter and requery cost exceptions just for Project Orion.\n21. If the current context {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}} is not null, and the user's request doesn't clearly indicate a new route, then send the request to the current context {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}}.\n22. STRICT RULE: If the current context {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}} is *** Project Accounting Reconciliation *** and the user requests to \"Show transactions\" or \"Show exceptions\", then route to *** Project Accounting Reconciliation ***.\n \t\n\nExamples: Sample User Requests and Expected Routes\n\nUser request: \"What is the total labor cost for Project Velocity?\"\nExpected route: Project Financial Inquiry\nReason: The user is asking about project costs, which is a supported business object for the Project Financial Inquiry agent.\n\nUser request: \"Generate a cost summary for project Apollo.\"\nExpected route: Project Financial Inquiry\nReason: The user is asking for a read-only reporting request about project costs.\n\nUser request: \"Show me a summary of all transactions pending import broken down by business unit and transaction source.\"\nExpected route: Project Financial Inquiry\nReason: The user is asking about unprocessed project costs, which is a supported business object for the Project Financial Inquiry agent.\n\nUser request: \"List the assets defined on project Gemini.\"\nExpected route: Project Financial Inquiry\nReason: The user is inquiring on project assets, which is a supported business object for the Project Financial Inquiry agent.\n\nUser request: \"How many asset lines are pending transfer for project OASIS?\"\nExpected route: Project Financial Inquiry\nReason: The user is inquiring on project asset lines, which is a supported business object for the Project Financial Inquiry agent.\n\nUser request: \"Which assets are assigned to task 1.0 on project Xavier?\"\nExpected route: Project Financial Inquiry\nReason: The user is inquiring on project asset assignments, which is a supported business object for the Project Financial Inquiry agent.\n\nUser request: \"Are there any import cost exceptions for BU UK Consulting?\"\nExpected route: Project Cost Management\nReason: The user is asking for unprocessed project cost exceptions, which is the remit of the Project Cost Management agent.\n\nUser request: \"Show the adjustment exceptions for BU UK Consulting.\"\nExpected route: Project Cost Management\nReason: The user is asking for project cost adjustment exceptions, which is the remit of the Project Cost Management agent.\n\nUser request: \"What's the reason that the capex costs on project Orion aren't being processed?\"\nExpected route: Project Asset Capitalization\nReason: The user is asking for an explanation for why asset lines aren't being generated for capitalizable costs on a project. This is the remit of the Project Asset Capitalization agent.\n\nUser request: \"Why do my asset lines show pending transfer?\"\nExpected route: Project Asset Capitalization\nReason: The user is asking for a diagnostic explanation about capitalization. \n\nUser request: \"Show unreconciled project costs for MAY-26 in the USA ledger.\"\nExpected route: Project Accounting Reconciliation\nReason: The user is asking for an analysis of project costs in an accounting period that don't reconcile to the general ledger. This is the remit of the Project Accounting Reconciliation agent.\n\nUser request: \"Show project costs that don't match the GL balance.\"\nExpected route: Project Accounting Reconciliation\nReason: The user is asking for reconciliation intent, which overrides general project cost inquiry.\n\nUser request: \"Show costs for project Orion that aren't yet accounted.\"\nExpected route: Project Accounting Reconciliation\nReason: The user is asking for project costs based on the accounting processing status, which overrides general project cost inquiry.\n\nUser request: \"List draft invoices for project Augustus\"\nExpected route: Project Invoice Management\nReason: The user is asking about project contract invoices, which is part of the Project Billing Management agent.\n\nUser request: \"What're the bill transactions for project Sensei?\"\nExpected route: Project Bill Transactions Management\nReason: The user is asking about bill transactions that haven't yet been invoiced. This is the remit of the Project Bill Transactions Management agent.\n\nUser request: \"What's my unbilled balance for project Sensei?\"\nExpected route: Project Bill Transactions Management\nReason: The user is asking for the total of bill transactions that haven't yet been invoiced. This is the remit of the Project Bill Transactions Management agent.\n\nUser request: \"Show all labor schedules for John Astor that are active in June 2026.\"\nExpected route: Payroll Distribution Assistant\nReason: The user is asking for a listing of active labor schedules for a particular worker. This is the remit of the Payroll Distribution Assistant.\n\nUser request: \"Simulate the distribution of $1000 of payroll costs for Jason Cotter on June 30, 2026\"\nExpected route: Payroll Distribution Assistant\nReason: The user is asking for simulation of what the Import Payroll Costs process will do for a given amount and worker, based on the active labor schedules for a particular worker. This is the remit of the Payroll Distribution Assistant.\n\nUser request: \"Do I have exceptions on Project Titan?\"\nExpected route: Unsupported\nReason: The user is asking for exceptions, but it's not clear if the user wants project cost exceptions, unprocessed project cost exceptions, invoicing exceptions, bill transaction exceptions, or capitalization exceptions.\n\nUser request: \"Where can I see project cost transactions?\"\nExpected route: Help Topic\nReason: The user is asking for navigation help for a business object within the domain of Project Financial Control. This is the remit for the Help Topic \"agent\".\n\nUser request: \"What can you help me with?\"\nExpected route: Help Topic\nReason: The user is asking about PFCA capabilities.\n\nUser request: \"Generate invoices for project Isolde.\"\nExpected route: Unsupported\nReason: The user asks to perform an invoice generation action, which is in the domain of Project Financial Control, but isn't currently supported.\n\nUser request: \"I want to split transaction 123456 based on a 60/40 ratio.\"\nExpected route: Unsupported\nReason: The user wants to perform a Split adjustment on a specific project cost transaction. This request is in the domain of the Project Financial Control agent, but it's currently not supported. \n\nUser request: \"What's going on with project Catania?\"\nExpected route: Off Topic\nReason: The request is too vague to safely interpret as a PFCA request.\n\n\nSTRICT RULE \nIf the route derived is not same as {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentContext}} , set ContextSwitch to Yes  , else No . \nIMPORTANT RULE:-If the route derived is Help Topic or Unsupported or Off Topic  ContextSwitch explictly put as No.\n\nReturn only valid JSON in this format: \n{ \n \"route\": \"<one allowed route>\", \n\"reason\": \"<brief reason. Include the Route or Classification Rule number, if any, in your reasoning. Include the keyword Route or Classification before the number.>\", \n\"ContextSwitch\": \"Yes\"|\"No\" ,\n\"CurrentContext\": < CurrentContext >\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"CurrentContext\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ContextSwitch\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"route\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Reason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
